p)"}]}, {"title": "Prompt String", "items": [{"t": "00:40", "x": "Types of shells"}, {"t": "01:55", "x": "Bash prompts (PS1, PS2, PS3, PS4)"}, {"t": "02:55", "x": "Escape Sequences in Prompt"}, {"t": "04:25", "x": "Python interactive mode prompts (ps1, ps2 in sys)"}, {"t": "04:55", "x": "$PS1"}, {"t": "06:55", "x": "\\t for time and \\d for date"}, {"t": "07:35", "x": "\\# to list command history number"}, {"t": "08:15", "x": "source ~/.bashrc to reset prompt"}, {"t": "09:00", "x": "$PS2 for unclosed brackets or quotes"}, {"t": "11:00", "x": "$PS3 for select loop prompt"}, {"t": "12:00", "x": "$PS4 for trace with set -x"}, {"t": "13:30", "x": "Python prompts sys.ps1 and sys.ps2"}]}, {"title": "Managing Storage", "items": [{"t": "0:49", "x": "Understanding logical volume management in Linux for efficient disk space allocation."}, {"t": "2:51", "x": "Data protection and storage optimization through RAID controllers and modes."}, {"t": "5:17", "x": "Importance of distributed parity in storage systems and benefits of RAID 6 for data protection."}, {"t": "7:58", "x": "Overview of RAID storage configurations and their benefits in managing storage."}, {"t": "10:47", "x": "Utilizing multiple hard disks to create a single, large storage volume for efficient access and management."}]}]}]